  "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the third equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{1} & =7-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ into the third equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 3(3)-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ -{x}_{2} & =4-9 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ -2(3)+3(5) & =9 \\\\ -6+15 & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.\n$$",
